  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response and Assistance to Displaced Population</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since May 2023, there has been an influx of Mauritanian returnees and Malian refugees to Mauritania as a result of the deteriorating security context in Mali. The increased pressure that returnee populations and their livestock have placed on the region&#x2019;s ecosystem, natural resources and socio-economic environment risks tension and conflict between returnees and host communities. In order to ensure community stability and social cohesion, it is essential to address the humanitarian needs of vulnerable returnees while considering the socio-economic needs of the host communities. 
 
With funding from the Government of Japan, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is promoting social cohesion and peaceful coexistence among returnees and host communities in the south of Mauritania by providing immediate humanitarian assistance to meet basic needs and enhancing the living conditions of Mauritanian returnees and host communities, as well as by improving the local capacity to respond more efficiently to emergencies, including natural hazards.</narrative>
  </description>
